# Moonlit Green - BONANZA's course 4 (SPEC.md 128.14.6): a night round of
# mini-golf, the course that teaches wave 4's FLAGS, the CUP and the PADS,
# glass last and gently.  Built for the RUBBER ball; every flag names its ball
# and `bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 7 proves from each flag and each pad, with
# its ball, that the cup can be reached (NO TRAP, 128.14.4.1).  In order:
#  1. the start tier (z 30) and an ICE approach between bumper rails; flag 0
#     at its corner (a pit beside it);
#  2. a steep ramp down to the STEEL pad; a corridor of STONE rails the route
#     zig-zags (steel's 0.13 restitution hugs a rail where rubber's 0.38
#     rattles off it) - OPTIONAL: a 2-unit drop beside its first stub skips
#     the second half for a 1 s stun (the STUN branch); the long flat COAST
#     straight down the screen;
#  3. the RUBBER pad and the rubber-only ledge: H, a 6-unit drop onto F four
#     tiles deep, a two-tile gap, G two units up (TRAIL's required bounce,
#     128.11.5.3); flag 1 in front of
#  4. the CLOWN MOUTH: a castle with three channels to three KEEP tubes - the
#     middle on to the course, the left a SHORTCUT under the terrace's rail to
#     the last green's foot (the SHORT branch), the right a DEAD END into a
#     walled pocket (RETURN is the way back from it);
#  5. flag 2 just before the GLASS pad; the glass TERRACE of one-unit steps
#     (glass bounces at lvz 312 and never shatters there), with one 3-unit
#     drop beside the line - a shatter there costs the way back to flag 2,
#     where the ball is rubber again (the flag's);
#  6. the last green, UP a gentle ramp so the ball arrives slow, sand round
#     the CUP (capture 160).
course MOON "Moonlit Green"
width 64
ball rubber
# 1 the start tier and the ice approach between bumper rails (z 30)
floor rect   5 10  8 13  flat 30
wall  rect   4  9  5 14  flat 31
floor rect   8 10 13 13  flat 30
surface ice rect 8 10 13 13
wall  rect   5  9 18 10  flat 31
wall  rect   5 13 13 14  flat 31
surface bounce rect 8 9 13 10
surface bounce rect 8 13 13 14
floor rect  13 10 17 15  flat 30
wall  rect  17  9 18 15  flat 31
hole  tile  16 13
checkpoint 14 11 ball rubber
# 2 down to the steel pad (z 24)
floor rect  13 15 17 19  ramp y 15 19 30 24
floor rect  13 19 17 22  flat 24
pad steel 14 20
# 3 the zig-zag corridor of stone rails (z 24); the optional drop to the lane (z 22)
floor rect  17 18 25 22  flat 24
wall  rect  17 17 26 18  flat 28
wall  rect  25 18 26 22  flat 25
wall  rect  18 18 19 20  flat 25
wall  rect  20 20 21 22  flat 25
wall  rect  22 18 23 20  flat 25
wall  rect  13 22 19 23  flat 25
wall  rect  20 22 23 23  flat 25
floor rect  19 22 20 24  flat 22
wall  rect  20 23 23 24  flat 25
floor rect  19 24 24 25  flat 22
floor rect  23 22 25 24  ramp y 22 24 24 22
# 4 the coast (z 22), straight down the screen, and the rubber pad
floor band   0 6 48 70  flat 22
wall  band  -2 -1 48 70  flat 23
wall  band   7 8 48 66  flat 23
# 5 H, the rubber pad, F six units down, the gap, G two units up
floor rect  37 31 40 36  flat 22
pad rubber 38 32
floor rect  37 36 40 40  flat 16
floor rect  37 42 40 45  flat 18
floor rect  38 45 40 47  flat 18
wall  rect  36 42 37 47  flat 18.5
wall  rect  37 47 41 48  flat 18.5
wall  tile  37 45  flat 18.5
wall  tile  37 46  flat 18.5
# 6 the castle: three channels, three KEEP tubes - the right a dead end, the
# middle on, the left a shortcut
floor rect  40 42 43 43  flat 18
floor rect  40 44 43 45  flat 18
floor rect  40 46 43 47  flat 18
wall  rect  40 43 43 44  flat 19
wall  rect  40 45 43 46  flat 19
wall  rect  43 41 45 48  flat 24
checkpoint 39 44 ball rubber
tube keep  42 42  45 42
tube keep  42 44  45 44
tube keep  42 46  52 47  via 44 46  via 44 47  out +x
# the dead end's pocket
floor rect  45 41 47 43  flat 18
wall  rect  45 40 48 41  flat 19
wall  rect  47 41 48 43  flat 19
# 7 the exit room, flag 2, the glass pad; the glass terrace east, a unit a step
floor rect  45 44 48 47  flat 18
wall  rect  45 43 49 44  flat 19
checkpoint 46 45 ball rubber
pad glass 47 45
floor rect  48 44 49 47  flat 17
floor rect  49 44 50 47  flat 16
floor rect  50 44 51 47  flat 15
floor rect  51 44 52 47  flat 14
wall  rect  45 47 52 48  flat 18.5
floor tile  49 43  flat 13
wall  tile  49 42  flat 14
wall  rect  50 43 52 44  flat 17
# 8 the last green: its foot, up a gentle ramp, the cup on the sand
floor rect  52 44 54 49  flat 14
floor tile  51 48  flat 14
floor rect  51 49 54 53  ramp y 49 53 14 16
floor rect  51 53 54 56  flat 16
surface sand rect 51 53 54 56
surface normal tile 52 54
cup 52 54
wall  rect  52 43 54 44  flat 15
wall  rect  54 44 55 57  flat 17
wall  rect  50 48 51 57  flat 17
wall  rect  51 56 54 57  flat 17

start 6 11

# The autopilot's route (the route demo's and bonanzaperf's leg, 128.14.6):
# along the ice to flag 0, down to the steel pad, through the zig-zag, down
# the coast to the rubber pad, off H's lip over the gap to G, flag 1, the
# middle tube, flag 2, the glass pad, the terrace and up the green to the cup
# - no fall (`bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 8).
way  6 11
way 14 11
way 14 20
way 17 20
way 19 19
way 21 20
way 23 21
way 24 23
way 27 27
way 31 31
way 36 31
way 38 32
way 38 43
way 39 44
way 40 44
way 42 44
way 45 44
way 46 45
way 47 45
way 51 45
way 52 46
way 52 51
way 52 54

# The OPTIONAL lines, the tool's alone (printed: the steps each saves and its
# hardest landing a ball): the stun drop beside the zig-zag, and the shortcut
# tube to the green's foot.
way 19 21 branch STUN
way 19 22 branch STUN
way 19 24 branch STUN
way 23 24 branch STUN
way 27 27 branch STUN
way 42 46 branch SHORT
way 52 47 branch SHORT
way 52 51 branch SHORT

# par: the autopilot's time on the route and a third (128.14.3.1, PROVISIONAL)
par 50
# Wave 5b (SPEC.md 128.15.8): the design time (CD3), the middle class until its retrofit; the
# course budget reads it (12550 bytes packed, refused past 1.5 times).  Tool-only:
# it writes nothing into the part, so no identity moves.
target 60
